  "tagline": "Open-source retrieval database for AI apps, from embedded Python to serverless Chroma Cloud.",
  "description": "Chroma started as the simplest way to add embeddings search to a Python notebook and became the default vector store in many LLM tutorials. The core was rewritten in Rust in 2025, and Chroma now offers dense, sparse (BM25/SPLADE), full-text and regex search, metadata filtering and collection forking. Locally it runs in-process or as a single server; Chroma Cloud is a serverless, object-storage-backed distributed version billed by data written, stored and queried. Ideal for getting RAG working quickly; evaluate the distributed story carefully for very large self-hosted deployments.",
